===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The day after the present day.
#: {{ux|en|'''Tomorrow''' will be sunny.}}
#* {{RQ:Kipling Light that Failed|page=70|passage='Go home, Nilghai,' said Dick; 'go home to your lonely little bed, and leave me in peace. I am about to turn in till '''to-morrow'''.'}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1926|title=Enough Rope|chapter=Godspeed|author=w:Dorothy Parker|page=69|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/enoughropepoems0000park/page/69/mode/1up|passage=Oh seek, my love, your newer way; / I'll not be left in sorrow. / So long as I have yesterday, / Go take your damned '''to-morrow'''!}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|countable}} A [[future]] [[period]] or [[time]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=American Flint|volume=55|year=1965|page=28|passage=It’s 1965 and we certainly welcome this new year with hopes that all of our '''tomorrows''' will bring happiness.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Alan S. Berger|quotee=“The doctor won’t be in today or tomorrow”|title=The City: Urban Communities and Their Problems|location=Dubuque, Ia.|publisher=Wm. C. Brown Company Publishers|year=1978|page=359|isbn=0-697-07555-9|passage=Surgoinsville, Tennessee, hasn’t had a doctor since 1965. That’s when the community’s only doctor died. Day after day, Surgoinsville’s modern medical clinic stands empty, useless. {{...}} Surgoinsville’s clinic faces a lot of empty '''tomorrows'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Chuck Robb|Charles S[pittal] Robb]]|chapter=The Age of Limits: Its Challenges and Opportunities|editor=Robert D. Behn|title=Governors on Governing|publisher=w:University Press of America|year=1991|page=10|isbn=0-8191-7890-X|passage=Additionally, programs such as our Televised Graduate Engineering Instruction effort, designed to allow engineers in the field to benefit from the latest research at our engineering schools, and the Continuous Electron Beam Accelerator Facility, which will spur research in high-energy-particle physics, will help Virginia as well as the entire Southeast enter the brave new high-tech world of '''tomorrow'''.}}

